D = {
"\"Leftovers\" Egg Bake|HFLOTT": "Mash butter with garlic, thyme, parsley, salt and pepper. Whisk eggs with half-and-half and seasoning. Layer buttered bread, leftovers and cheese twice in a greased 2-quart dish. Pour the egg mixture over, press down, cover and weigh it. Chill 3 to 24 hours, then rest 30 minutes. Bake at 350°F for about 55 minutes until puffed. Cool 10 minutes, cut into squares and serve warm.",
"\"Orc\" Bacon|HF": "Heat the oven to 375°F. Lay a pound of bacon on a greased rack over a foil-lined sheet. Roast about 12 minutes. Brush with half of a brown sugar, pepper, garlic powder and orange juice glaze and roast about 7 minutes. Flip, brush with the rest and roast 5 to 7 minutes more until glossy. Serve warm.",
"Abyssal Chicken Egg Omelet|HFLOTT": "Broil poblano halves 12 to 15 minutes until blackened, steam 10 minutes, then peel and chop. Heat the oven to 400°F. Beat eggs with salt, pepper and smoked paprika. Cook bacon about 8 minutes in an oven-safe skillet, then soften onion 3 to 4 minutes. Add poblanos and bacon, pour in the eggs, set the edges 1 minute, then bake about 14 minutes. Cool 15 minutes and slice.",
"Ale and Cheese Pastry|HFLOTT": "Heat the oven to 425°F. Boil ale, butter and seasoning, then stir in flour off the heat. Beat over low heat for 3 minutes. Process the dough with eggs, then cheese. Scoop 16 mounds onto a lined sheet, smooth them and brush with egg yolk wash. Bake about 30 minutes, turning the sheet halfway. Serve warm.",
"Almond Brandy|PAF": "Shake brandy, amaretto, lime juice and bitters with ice for about 30 seconds until chilled. Strain into two cocktail glasses and serve at once.",
"Amphail Braised Beef|HF": "Brown tied, seasoned beef about 14 minutes total. Cook onions with salt 4 minutes, then gently 15 minutes, then 5 minutes with thyme, ginger and flour. Add cider and broth, nestle in the beef and braise covered at 300°F for 1 hour 35 minutes. Add pears and cook about 2¼ hours more until the beef hits 200°F. Skim the juices, add vinegar and parsley, slice and serve.",
"Apple Apple Frycakes|HFLOTT": "Grate one apple with sugar and drain 30 minutes. Slice two apples into ¼-inch rings. Whisk wet and dry batter parts, then fold in the grated apple. Heat the oven to 200°F. Dip rings in batter and fry on medium-low about 2½ minutes per side until golden. Keep warm in the oven. Roll each cake in cinnamon sugar and serve.",
"Arkhan the Cruel's Flame-Roasted Halfling Chili|HF": "Mix the spices. Puree half the beans with broth. Fry bacon about 13 minutes, then soften onion 4 minutes. Cook garlic and spices 1 minute. Add broth, tomato puree, sugar, bean puree, turkey and remaining beans. Simmer about 30 minutes. Stir in vinegar and bacon, adjust seasoning and serve with crackers, cheese and onion.",
"Astral Plane|PAF": "Shake gin, violet liqueur, elderflower liqueur, lemon juice and edible glitter with ice for 30 seconds. Strain into two chilled coupe or martini glasses and serve at once.",
"Bacon-Wrapped Smoked Mussels|HFFOTM": "Heat the oven to 400°F. Cook bacon on medium-low about 8 minutes, then halve the slices. Wrap two mussels in each half slice and pin with a toothpick. Roast on a rack about 8 minutes until browned and crisp. Rest 1 minute and serve hot.",
"Baldurian Tonic|PAF": "Steep Earl Grey tea bags in boiled water for 6 minutes. Dissolve sugar in it, boil, then simmer 5 minutes and cool for a syrup. Keeps 1 week in the fridge. Fill two highball glasses with ice. Add 2 ounces syrup, 2 ounces lemon juice and 3 ounces tonic water to each. Stir and serve.",
"Bangers and Smash|HF": "Roast potatoes at 450°F for about 40 minutes, cool 10 minutes, then press flat to 1 inch and oil them. Roast 15 minutes, turn, and add oiled leeks and sausages. Roast 8 minutes, stir the leeks and add oiled tomatoes. Roast about 10 minutes more until skins burst and potatoes crisp. Top with parsley.",
"Barovian Butterscotch Pudding|HF": "Boil butter, brown sugar, water, corn syrup, lemon juice and salt to 240°F, then simmer to 300 to 310°F. Carefully whisk in some cream-milk, then the rest, and heat to a simmer. Temper in egg yolks and cornstarch and cook 1 minute. Add vanilla and Scotch, strain, cover and chill 4 to 24 hours. Stir and top with whipped cream.",
"Barovian Garlic Bread|HFFOTM": "Heat the oven to 475°F. Cook garlic in butter and water 8 to 10 minutes, add more butter and steep 10 minutes, then strain and salt. Cut pizza dough into 12 pieces, roll into ropes and tie knots. Bake about 5 minutes, brush with half the butter, bake about 7 minutes more. Brush with the rest, salt and cool 5 minutes.",
"Barovian Garlic Soup|HFLOTT": "Toast bread cubes in olive oil about 5 minutes. Cook garlic 1 minute, then paprika and cayenne about 40 seconds. Add broth and water and simmer about 10 minutes, mashing the bread. Add vinegar, salt, pepper and parsley. Drizzle in whisked eggs while stirring so they form strands. Top with olive oil and parsley.",
"Beauty Mark|PAF": "Crush 2 teaspoons of pink peppercorns, add sherry and vermouth and infuse 15 minutes. Stir with ice for 30 seconds. Strain into two coupe glasses and garnish each with ¼ teaspoon peppercorns.",
"Bee Well|PAF": "Muddle ginger in a shaker. Add mead, orange liqueur, lemon juice, honey and egg whites and shake 1 minute. Add ice and shake 30 seconds. Strain into two old-fashioned glasses, share the foam and garnish with honeycomb.",
"Beer \"Porridge\"|HFLOTT": "Toast oats 4 to 5 minutes and cool. Soak dates and oats in warm water about 30 minutes, then drain. Blend dates with coffee for about 30 seconds. Add oats, vanilla and a pinch of salt and blend at least 30 seconds. Pulse in the beer and dust with nutmeg.",
"Beer Bread|HFFOTM": "Heat the oven to 375°F. Whisk the dry ingredients, stir in beer to a lumpy batter and pour into a greased 9 by 5-inch pan. Drizzle with 2 tablespoons melted butter. Bake about 55 minutes, brushing with the remaining butter halfway. Cool 10 minutes in the pan and 20 on a rack.",
"Beluir Poached Salmon|HFFOTM": "Steam a salmon fillet skin-side down over boiling water for 6 to 9 minutes until just translucent, then cool and flake. Blend cream cheese, lemon juice, paprika, cayenne, salt and pepper, then half the salmon. Fold in the rest with shallots, smoked salmon and chives. Chill about 30 minutes. Rest briefly and serve with crostini and capers.",
"Bigby's Brew|HFLOTT": "Layer mandarins, kiwi, cantaloupe, star fruit, strawberries and blueberries in a clear bowl and top with pineapple spears. Shake brandy, rum, Grand Marnier, lemon juice and syrup with ice for at least 15 seconds. Pour over the fruit, cover loosely and chill about 4 hours. Serve, mixing or digging to the bottom.",
"Bitter Black|PAF": "Pour 12 ounces of stout into each of two pint glasses. Add half the espresso and half the maple syrup to each, stir gently and serve at once.",
"Black Lotus Root|HFFOTM": "Soak sliced lotus 15 minutes. Boil in salted water about 1½ minutes, then plunge into ice water. Simmer vinegar, water and sugar, then whisk in butterfly pea powder and salt. Add lotus and shallot and cool 30 minutes. Refrigerate at least 24 hours and up to 5 days until deep purple. Serve cold.",
"Black Pudding|HF": "Whisk brown sugar, espresso powder, cocoa, cornstarch and salt. Add yolks, cream and milk. Cook on medium, whisking, 8 to 10 minutes until thick and bubbling, then 1 minute more. Off heat, whisk in butter, vanilla, coffee liqueur and brandy. Strain, cover the surface and chill 4 to 12 hours. Stir and top with chocolate shavings and cream.",
"Blackroot Tal with Honey|HFLOTT": "Boil 16 ounces of water per drinker. Warm the teapot and cups with some of it for 2 minutes each, then empty them. Put a heaping teaspoon of tea per drinker in the infuser with 8 to 10 ounces of water each. Steep 4 to 5 minutes. Pour into warmed cups, sweeten with honey and serve at once.",
"Blood of Vol|HFFOTM": "Brown salami in olive oil about 3 minutes and set aside. Cook onion, bell peppers, bay leaf and salt about 20 minutes. Add garlic, paprika, thyme and pepper flakes for 45 seconds, then salami and tomatoes. Cook about 5 minutes more and finish with vinegar and parsley. Scramble whisked eggs about 2 minutes in oil and spoon them over the peppers.",
"Boar Hock Soup|HFFOTM": "Brown seasoned pork about 4 minutes per side, then cut into ¾-inch pieces. Cook carrots, onions, herbs and fennel 5 minutes, then covered 6 minutes. Add garlic for 40 seconds, then broth and pork. Simmer covered 40 minutes. Add potatoes, leeks and chestnuts and simmer 20 minutes. Rest 30 minutes. Blend some soup with chestnuts, stir back in with vinegar and parsley.",
"Brackleberry Jam|HFFOTM": "Chill a plate. Boil strawberries, blueberries, blackberries, sugar, lemon juice and salt for 5 minutes, then mash. Boil 15 to 18 minutes more until slightly thick. Test a spoonful on the cold plate. If the trail does not hold, simmer 2 to 4 minutes more. Cool in a jar and refrigerate up to 3 weeks.",
"Braised Lamb|HF": "Sizzle olive oil, garlic, thyme and rosemary 3 to 4 minutes. Rub most of it on trimmed, scored lamb, then roll, tie and rest 1 hour. Heat the oven to 400°F. Brown the lamb about 12 minutes, then roast about 40 minutes to 120 to 125°F for medium-rare. Rest 15 minutes. Simmer pearl onions in vermouth 5 minutes, add sugar and herbs 4 minutes, then butter, lemon and mint.",
"Brandied Ham and Carrots|HFLOTT": "Heat the oven to 450°F. Toss carrots with oil, cumin, paprika and salt. Roast covered about 10 minutes. Whisk orange juice concentrate, honey, brandy and tomato paste. Lay a ham steak on the carrots and brush with half. Roast 7 to 9 minutes, flip, brush with the rest and roast 7 to 9 minutes more. Top with scallions.",
"Brandy Cassalanter|PAF": "Shake brandy, crème de banana, coconut milk and chocolate bitters with ice for about 30 seconds. Strain through a fine-mesh strainer into 2 cocktail glasses and serve at once.",
"Breaded Bird Cutlets|HFFOTM": "Heat the oven to 200°F. Slice two chicken breasts into eight cutlets, pound to ¼ to ½ inch, season and rest 10 minutes. Flour, egg and fry them about 2 minutes per side, keeping them warm in the oven. Soften shallot and thyme 2 minutes, reduce vermouth about 2½ minutes, add broth and lemon and reduce about 3 minutes. Whisk in floured butter and parsley and spoon over the cutlets.",
"Butternut Beer|HFFOTM": "Half fill two frosted mugs with ice. Add to each 1½ ounces rye, ¾ ounce schnapps, 1 teaspoon lemon juice and 3 drops bitters and stir. Add 2 ounces seltzer and 4 ounces cream soda to each, stir gently and garnish with lemon slices.",
"Bytopian Shepherd's Bread|HF": "Heat the oven to 350°F and grease an 8½ by 4½-inch pan. Whisk the dry ingredients with currants. Whisk eggs, brown sugar, butter, buttermilk and vanilla, then stir in carrots. Fold in the dry mix without overmixing. Top with almonds. Bake about 55 minutes, turning halfway. Cool 15 minutes in the pan, then on a rack.",
"Candied Phase Spider Eyes|HFLOTT": "Stir grape and lemon juice, sprinkle gelatin on top and rest 5 minutes. Add honey and warm on low about 4 minutes without boiling. Add a pinch of salt and food coloring, skim foam and fill candy molds. Chill at least 45 minutes until very firm. Unmold and serve. They keep about a week refrigerated.",
"Candlekeep Tea|PAF": "Combine gin, orange liqueur, red vermouth, lemon juice and bitters in a pitcher. Boil water, add tea bags, orange slices, cloves, cinnamon stick and sugar, then turn off the heat and steep 4 to 6 minutes. Strain into the pitcher, stir, pour into tea cups and garnish with lemon slices.",
"Captain's Fancy|PAF": "Whip cream to soft peaks with confectioners' sugar and cinnamon and chill up to 2 hours. Brown butter about 3 minutes. Stir in brown sugar, cinnamon, allspice, vanilla, dark rum and hot water. Divide between heatproof mugs, top with the cream and serve at once.",
"Caster's Stew|HFLOTT": "Heat the oven to 325°F. Brown floured venison in batches, about 2 minutes per side. Cook onion, carrots and bay leaves 6 minutes, tomato paste 2 minutes, then garlic and herbs 1 minute. Add wine and broth, return the venison and bake 30 minutes. Add carrots and turnips, bake about 1½ hours more. Cook mushrooms about 10 minutes with chestnuts, garlic and wine, then stir in with vinegar.",
"Castle Amber Onion Soup|HF": "Cook onions in butter about 10 minutes, then with bay leaves about 1½ hours until gold. Deglaze with ¼ cup water three more times, about 12 minutes each. Add thyme and flour 3 minutes, then sherry 3 minutes. Add broths and simmer 30 minutes. Bake baguette slices at 425°F for 10 minutes, top with Gruyère and broil about 4 minutes. Float on the soup with chives.",
"Cat's Cradle|PAF": "Toast cloves, cardamom, cinnamon, star anise and coriander 2 to 3 minutes. Muddle with lemon peels and sugar 30 seconds. Add lemon juice, tea, pineapple juice, whiskey and bitters and infuse at least 1 hour. Pour into hot milk, which curdles. Cool, then chill 1 to 24 hours. Strain slowly through a coffee filter over several hours. Pour about 4 ounces over large ice cubes in two rocks glasses.",
"Celebration Brew|PAF": "Shake rum, orange liqueur, lemon juice and orange juice with ice for about 30 seconds. Strain into two tulip glasses. Top each with ¾ cup of lager, stir gently, garnish with orange slices and serve at once.",
"Cheap Seat|PAF": "Spread 1 teaspoon of almond butter inside the rim of two cocktail glasses. Shake vodka, dark crème de cacao, amaro, Irish cream and bitters with ice for about 30 seconds. Strain into the glasses, dust with cocoa powder and serve at once.",
"Cherry Mead|PAF": "Combine mead, cherry juice, maraschino liqueur, rose water and vanilla in a large pitcher. Add ice, stir and serve at once in rocks or stemless wine glasses.",
"Cherrybread|HF": "Warm raisins with rum in the microwave about 1 minute, then let them soak covered for 1 hour and drain. Heat the oven to 300°F and line a buttered 9 by 5-inch pan with parchment. Toss dry ingredients with apricots, cherries, raisins and walnuts. Fold in eggs, molasses and vanilla. Bake about 1 hour, turning halfway and tenting if it browns too fast. Cool fully, then slice thinly.",
"Chessentan Tea|PAF": "Simmer sugar, water and jalapeños 3 minutes, steep 10 minutes, strain and cool. It keeps 1 week in the fridge. Steep tea bags in 2 cups of boiling water for 6 minutes and cool 5 minutes. In an iced pitcher, mix the tea, 2 more cups of water, ⅓ cup syrup, lime juice and orange juice. Serve over ice with flowers and jalapeño slices.",
"Chicken-Something Dumplings|HF": "Brown chicken thighs about 5 minutes per side and skin them. Soften sliced leek with thyme, bay leaves, garlic and flour, add sherry and broth, return the chicken and simmer covered about 1 hour. Shred the meat back in. Mix dumpling dough with scallions and warm milk and butter. Add carrots, celery and leek pieces, drop 12 dumplings on top and cook covered on low 15 to 20 minutes.",
"Chickpea and Spicy Sausage Soup|HFFOTM": "Brown chouriço in olive oil 5 to 6 minutes and set aside, saving the oil. Cook onion, celery and bay leaves 3 minutes, then covered 4 minutes. Add garlic and pepper flakes 40 seconds. Add broth, water, tomato sauce and chickpeas with their liquid. Simmer covered about 40 minutes. Return the sausage, add parsley and drizzle with the reserved oil.",
"Chirper's Sugar Biscuits|HFFOTM": "Mix lemon zest, sugars, cinnamon, cardamom and salt, saving 2 tablespoons. Roll puff pastry to 15 inches, spread with butter and the sugar mix, and roll tightly. Chill about 45 minutes. Heat the oven to 400°F. Cut into 12 pieces and set in a muffin tin. Bake about 20 minutes. Brush with melted butter, sprinkle with reserved sugar and cool 3 minutes in the tin.",
"Chocolate Scones with Yak Butter|HFLOTT": "Pulse cocoa, flour, sugar, leaveners, salt, cinnamon and espresso powder, then grated butter. Add chocolate chips, then egg, cream and vanilla. Pat into two 6-inch circles, cut into 6 wedges each and chill 30 minutes. Bake at 400°F about 15 minutes after a 500°F preheat. Cool 10 minutes, dip tops in a vanilla glaze and set 15 minutes. Serve with honey butter.",
"Chopforest|HFFOTM": "Salt cabbage in a colander for 1 to 4 hours, rinse and dry it well. Whisk olives, vinegar, lemon zest, garlic, salt and pepper, then stream in olive oil. Toss the cabbage with fennel bulb, scallions, parsley and the dressing. Top with fennel fronds.",
"Chultan Zombie|HF": "Shake rum, pineapple juice, orange juice, grenadine, lime juice, Cointreau and bitters with ice for 30 seconds. Strain into two iced Collins or highball glasses. Add 1½ ounces seltzer to each if wanted, stir gently, garnish and serve at once.",
"Chultwater|PAF": "Fill a large bowl three-quarters with ice. Add blue curaçao, dark rum, light rum, falernum, lemon juice, pineapple juice, orange juice and passion fruit and stir. Garnish with mint and basil and serve at once in rocks glasses.",
"Cloaks|HFFOTM": "Microwave potatoes about 18 minutes, stirring twice, and cool 5 minutes. Rice them, then stir in half the butter, half-and-half, seasoning, egg, yolks and baking powder. Cool, then fold in the remaining butter. Heat the oven to 475°F. Pipe 20 mounds, about 2 inches wide and tall, onto a greased lined sheet. Bake about 14 minutes, rotating halfway. Cool 2 minutes and serve.",
"Cocoa Broth|HF": "Whisk cocoa, brown sugar, cinnamon, cardamom, salt and water over medium heat. Simmer about 2 minutes, whisking. Whisk in milk and heat about 10 minutes without boiling. Add vanilla and espresso, adjust the sweetness and pour into four mugs. Add marshmallow if wanted.",
"Community Cheeses|HF": "Blanch broccoli or cauliflower about 4 minutes, chill in ice water and dry. Thicken simmered wine and garlic with a cornstarch slurry for 15 to 30 seconds, add lemon juice, then melt Gruyère and Emmental in ½-cup batches over about 8 minutes. Cook about 4 minutes more until smooth and just bubbling, never boiling. Add Kirsch, nutmeg and salt. Serve in a garlic-rubbed fondue pot with the dippers.",
"Corn and Lentil Soup|HFLOTT": "Brown zucchini about 3 minutes, then corn about 3 minutes, and set both aside. Soften onions with bay leaves about 4 minutes, then covered 3 minutes. Cook tomato paste 2 minutes, then cumin, coriander, cayenne and garlic 1 minute. Add broth, water and tomatoes, then lentils. Simmer covered about 35 minutes, adding zucchini and corn at 25 minutes. Finish with cilantro and lime juice.",
"Corned Beef and Cabbage|HF": "Heat the oven to 300°F. Cook corned beef covered with garlic, pickling spice, onion, carrots, celery, broth and water about 4 hours. Rest the meat in a cup of liquid 30 minutes. Skim the strained liquid, add potatoes and simmer covered about 8 minutes. Add cabbage and simmer 10 to 14 minutes, turning at 6 minutes. Slice the meat, toss vegetables with butter and serve with parsley.",
"Courtesans|PAF": "Soften goat cheese about 1 hour. Cut an X in each fig three-quarters through and salt them. Heat the oven to 400°F. Mix the cheese with 1 teaspoon honey, pistachios, salt and pepper and stuff the figs. Drizzle with olive oil and bake 5 to 7 minutes until soft and juicy. Drizzle with the remaining honey and pepper and serve warm or cold.",
"Crakaneg|PAF": "Beat egg yolks 1 to 2 minutes, then beat in sugar until pale. Steam milk with cloves, cinnamon and vanilla to 155°F. Whisk the milk into the yolks, return to the pan and cook about 5 minutes to 160°F until it coats a spoon. Stir in cream, strain, add brandy and nutmeg. Cool 1 hour, then chill at least 1 hour. Keeps 1 week.",
"Craknoeg|PAF": "Blend cashew milk, coconut cream, dates, maple syrup, vanilla, cinnamon, nutmeg, cloves and salt on high for 1 to 2 minutes. Stir in brandy and chill at least 1 hour. Serve with grated nutmeg. It keeps 1 week in a jar in the fridge.",
"Create Food and Water|HFLOTT": "Slice tofu into ½-inch slabs, press under towels and a weight for at least 20 minutes. Whisk soy sauce, sesame oil, maple syrup, rice vinegar, 1 tablespoon water, gochujang, ginger and garlic. Coat the tofu in the marinade, cover and refrigerate 8 hours, turning once halfway. Top with sesame seeds and scallions.",
"Cremfels|HFLOTT": "Blend flour, sugar, salt, eggs, milk and rum into batter and rest 15 minutes. Whip cream with honey, crème fraîche and vanilla to firm peaks and chill. Blend melted butter into the batter. Cook thin 7-inch crepes about 1 minute, then 45 to 60 seconds on the other side. Fill each with creme, fold into quarters and serve with more creme and raspberries.",
"Curtie's Special|HFLOTT": "Whisk gochugaru, gochujang, soy sauce, fish sauce, sugar, garlic and ¼ cup broth. Arrange onion, SPAM, hot dogs, tofu, mushrooms and kimchi in piles in a wide pot. Add the sauce, remaining broth and 1 cup water. Boil covered about 8 minutes, then simmer partly covered about 10 minutes. Add noodles 1½ minutes, then scallion greens and cheese 2 minutes. Add scallion whites and serve with rice.",
"Dark Molasses Nutbread|HF": "Heat the oven to 350°F and prepare an 8½ by 4½-inch pan. Whisk the flours, cornmeal, leaveners and salt, then stir in walnuts. Whisk buttermilk, molasses and melted butter, and fold into the dry mix without overmixing. Bake 40 to 45 minutes, turning halfway. Cool 20 minutes in the pan, then on a rack. Slice with a serrated knife.",
"Deadwinter Fire|PAF": "Simmer water, sugar, habanero and lime zest 5 minutes, cool 10 minutes and strain. It keeps 1 week in the fridge. Fill two highball glasses three-quarters with ice. Divide lime juice, 1 ounce of syrup, grapefruit juice and tequila between them. Top with soda water, stir gently and garnish with a slit grapefruit wheel.",
"Deep Gnome Trillimac Pods|HF": "Brown cremini about 12 minutes, add half the onion 4 minutes, half the garlic 1 minute, then sherry 1 minute. Add parsley and cool. Cook the rest of the onion and garlic and mix with ricotta, egg, ½ cup Parmesan and ground dried mushroom. Heat the oven to 375°F. Layer wonton wrappers and both fillings in a muffin tin, top with cheese. Bake about 20 minutes.",
"Delayed Blast Fireball|HF": "Infuse bourbon with red pepper flakes and cinnamon sticks in a lidded jar for 5 days, shaking daily. Dissolve brown sugar in hot water and cool about 10 minutes. Strain the bourbon through cheesecloth into it. Pour the mix back into the jar with the firestar wine. Serve, or store in a cool, dark place up to 3 months.",
"Delzoun \"Tide-Me-Overs\"|HF": "Soak bread in cream and egg about 20 minutes and mash. Soften onion 4 minutes, add allspice 40 seconds and cool. Mix with pork and beef, form tablespoon balls and bake at 475°F about 20 minutes. Brown butter 1 to 2 minutes, cook in flour 2 to 3 minutes, whisk in broth 2 minutes, add sugar, soy sauce and lemon juice 2 minutes. Simmer the meatballs 4 minutes with dill.",
"Double-High Halfling Pie|HFLOTT": "Heat the oven to 350°F. Bake a graham cracker crust in a 9-inch deep dish 12 to 15 minutes. Cook raspberry filling about 2 minutes, then 1 minute after it boils, cool 15 minutes, fold in fresh berries and chill at least 4 hours. Cook mango filling about 4½ plus 5 minutes, cool 30 minutes, layer on and chill at least 4 hours. Top with whipped cream.",
"Dour Bread|HFLOTT": "Warm milk and butter to 105 to 110°F. Mix with flour, sugar, yeast, salt, eggs and vanilla, then knead 8 to 10 minutes. Rise 60 to 90 minutes. Cut ten balls, rest 30 minutes, flatten to 4 to 5 inches and rise under a second sheet about 45 minutes. Heat the oven to 400°F. Bake 9 minutes, flip, bake 6 to 9 minutes more. Keeps 3 days.",
"Dragon Salmon|HF": "Heat the oven to 200°F. Season salmon and sear flesh-side down 3 to 4 minutes, then skin-side down 3 minutes for rare or 4 for medium. Keep warm tented in the oven. Soften shallot and thyme in butter 1 minute. Add wine and broth and reduce by about two-thirds, 6 to 8 minutes. Off heat swirl in butter and salt. Pour over the salmon and top with chives.",
"Dragonberries|PAF": "Heat the oven to 425°F. Pat canned chickpeas dry and toss with cumin, paprika, chili powder, coriander, garlic powder, onion powder, cayenne, salt and olive oil. Spread on a foil-lined sheet and bake 25 to 35 minutes until crispy. Cool fully before serving.",
"Dragonfire Mead|HFLOTT": "Rim two glasses with lime juice and Tajín. Muddle chile slices with sugar in a shaker. Add 2 ounces of lime juice, honey syrup, mezcal and mead with ice and shake at least 15 seconds. Pour over ice in the glasses, garnish with lime slices and serve at once.",
"Drow Mushroom Steaks|HF": "Whisk olive oil, lemon juice, balsamic vinegar, thyme, salt and pepper. Marinate mushrooms at room temperature for 15 minutes, turning once. Grill on medium-high heat 10 to 12 minutes, flipping, until tender and browned. Serve hot or at room temperature.",
"Druid Winter Cocktail|HFLOTT": "Stand a rosemary sprig in each lime half and press one into the bottom of each of two tall glasses. Fill halfway with ice. Pour 2 ounces of gin into each. Stir tonic with edible glitter in a third glass and split it between them. Garnish with lime slices and swizzle sticks and serve at once. Guests stir to shimmer the drink.",
"Duergar Smoked Herring|HFFOTM": "Cook onion, red bell pepper, Cubanelle pepper, Scotch bonnet and salt in oil about 5 minutes. Add tomato paste about 1½ minutes, then thyme and garlic 40 seconds, then tomatoes about 3 minutes. Add kippers and warm them about 3 minutes without shredding. Stir in scallions and lime juice, discard the chile and serve with a lime wedge.",
"Duskmallow Pie|HFLOTT": "Heat the oven to 350°F. Press gingersnap crumbs with brown sugar and melted butter into a 9-inch pan and bake about 12 minutes. Melt milk and marshmallows 4 to 6 minutes, stir in cream cheese and vanilla about 2 minutes, then cool about 25 minutes. Fold in whipped cream, fill the crust and chill at least 4 hours. Top with chopped gingersnaps.",
"Dwarven Flatbread|HF": "Whisk flour, baking powder, baking soda, salt and herbs. Stir in olive oil and yogurt, knead smooth, divide into eight balls and rest 15 minutes. Keep the oven at 200°F. Roll each ball into a 7-inch circle. Cook in oil on medium heat 3 to 4 minutes per side until spotty brown. Keep warm in the oven and serve fresh.",
"Dwarven Mulled Wine|HF": "Peel orange zest in strips, saving one per drink, and stud some with cloves. Juice the oranges. Simmer the juice with brown sugar, then add wine, cinnamon stick and zest. Simmer partly covered about 1 hour without boiling. Add vanilla and brandy for 2 minutes, then remove the solids. Ladle into preheated mugs and garnish with the saved zest.",
"Eel Rolls with Sticky Rice|HFLOTT": "Reduce mirin, sake, soy sauce and agave into eel sauce, about 8 to 10 minutes. Rinse rice, soak 30 minutes, simmer covered about 6 minutes, cook on low 12 minutes and rest 12 minutes. Fold in sushi vinegar and rest 15 minutes. Broil eel slices 9 to 10 minutes. Roll nori, rice, sauce, eel, cucumber, chile and ginger on a mat, cut into 8 pieces each, and dab with sauce.",
"Eggplant Steaks with Harelveauplum Sauce|HFLOTT": "Salt eggplant slices and drain 1 hour, then blot dry. Heat oiled sheets at 425°F. Bread the slices in flour, egg and seasoned panko. Bake 20 minutes, flip and bake 20 to 25 minutes more. For the sauce, soften onion and bell pepper about 6 minutes, cook plums about 7 minutes with water, add garlic and chile 40 seconds, then vinegar and honey 1 minute. Add herbs and spoon over.",
"Eldeen Banquet|HFFOTM": "Salt eggplant slices and drain 1 hour, then blot dry. Heat oiled sheets at 425°F. Bread the slices in flour, egg and seasoned panko. Bake 20 minutes, flip and bake 20 to 25 minutes more. For the topping, soften shallot 2 minutes, add garlic 40 seconds, then tomatoes and sugar about 4 minutes. Toss with vinegar and parsley and spoon over the eggplant.",
"Eldritch Storm|PAF": "Brown butter about 5 minutes, stir in miso and rum, cool and shake in a jar. Chill 1 to 2 hours until the butter solidifies, then strain it out. Fill two highball glasses with ice and divide coffee liqueur, ginger beer and lime juice between them. Float the miso rum on top for three layers. Garnish with lime and ginger and serve at once.",
"Elfharrow Baked Goat Cheese|HFFOTM": "Grind Melba toast with salt and pepper, add ¼ cup shallots. Dip goat cheese slices in egg and mustard, coat with crumbs and freeze about 45 minutes. Whisk vinegar, lemon juice, mustard, salt, pepper and ¼ cup shallots, rest 10 minutes, then stream in olive oil. Bake the oiled cheese at 475°F for 9 to 14 minutes. Cool 2 minutes and serve on dressed greens with chives.",
"Elfharrow Kiss|PAF": "Shake mezcal, Campari, elderflower liqueur, lime juice and simple syrup with ice for 30 seconds. Strain into two coupe glasses, garnish with edible flowers and serve at once.",
"Elven Bread|HF": "Dissolve yeast in ¼ cup warm milk. Mix with more milk, honey, 2 eggs, butter, salt and both flours, then knead about 8 minutes by machine. Rise 1 hour. Roll each half to 6 by 20 inches, brush with egg wash, add cinnamon sugar and roll up. Rise 1½ to 2 hours in loaf pans. Bake at 400°F for 10 minutes, then 350°F for 25 to 30 minutes. Cool.",
"Elven Flatbread|HFFOTM": "Mix flour, yeast, salt and water into a sticky dough and refrigerate 12 to 48 hours. Move it to an oiled 13 by 9-inch dish and rise 2½ to 4 hours. Heat the oven to 425°F. Oil and dimple the dough, press on vegetables, brush with oil and add herbs and flaky salt. Bake 28 to 40 minutes, turning halfway. Cool 15 minutes in the pan.",
"Elven Marruth|HF": "Roast diced onion, potato, carrots and cabbage in oil at 375°F for 25 to 30 minutes, then add thyme and cool 20 minutes. Season with soy sauce and dill. Roll pastry into 12-inch circles pressed with thyme leaves and cut twelve 4-inch rounds. Fill each with 1½ tablespoons, fold, seal and crimp. Brush with egg wash. Bake about 25 minutes, switching racks halfway. Cool 5 minutes.",
"Elverquisst|HFFOTM": "Dissolve sugar in water in a pitcher. Add wine, both juices, Calvados and cinnamon sticks. Cover and chill 4 to 24 hours. Remove the cinnamon, add seltzer and ice, and stir. Pour over ice and garnish each glass with an apple slice if wanted.",
"Emerald Chicken|HFFOTM": "Season chicken breasts under the skin and chill. Heat the oven to 325°F. Char tomatillos, onion, garlic and chiles 6 minutes per side, then blend with cilantro, lime juice, sugar and salt into salsa. Brown the chicken 3 to 4 minutes, then roast to 160°F, 25 to 40 minutes. Rest 5 minutes. Wilt spinach with garlic about 4 minutes. Sear chicken livers about 2½ plus 2 minutes. Plate with salsa.",
"Emerald Door|PAF": "Boil sugar, matcha and water, stir to dissolve and cool for a syrup. It keeps 1 week in the fridge. Muddle mint in lemon juice. Add gin, elderflower liqueur and ½ ounce of syrup with ice and shake about 30 seconds. Strain into two flutes of crushed ice, top with sparkling wine and garnish with mint.",
"Endurance|PAF": "Muddle mint and strawberries in a shaker. Add simple syrup and brandy with ice and shake about 30 seconds. Swirl ¼ ounce of absinthe in each of two highball glasses and pour out the excess. Fill with crushed ice, strain in the drink, top with club soda and garnish with mint and a strawberry.",
"Evermead|HF": "Warm cinnamon sticks and cloves about 2 minutes. Add water and ginger and simmer. Whisk in honey, jam and a pinch of salt. Simmer partly covered on low about 20 minutes, then steep covered 20 minutes. Strain. Serve warm, at room temperature or lightly chilled.",
"Everything Soup|HF": "Infuse 3 tablespoons of butter with rosemary and garlic about 1 minute. Soften onion, carrots, red pepper and herbs in the other butter about 5 minutes, then covered 8 minutes. Add broth and potato, simmer about 5 minutes. Add green beans about 3 minutes, then leek, corn and chicken about 3 minutes more. Drizzle each serving with the strained butter.",
"Eye Of The Beholder|PAF": "Freeze lychees in a Bundt pan with lychee liquid and water for several hours, saving ¾ cup of liquid. Unmold by dipping in warm water. Dissolve citric acid in orange juice. In a punch bowl, stir melon liqueur, tequila, orange liqueur, saved lychee liquid, lime juice, the orange juice and agave. Top with club soda, add the ring and garnish with orange and blackberry.",
"Faerie Cake|HFLOTT": "Beat cream cheese with jam, vanilla and salt, then chill. Heat the oven to 350°F. Beat flour, baking powder, salt, sugar and butter to a mealy mix, then eggs, milk and vanilla for about 3 minutes. Bake 12 cakes 18 to 22 minutes, turning halfway. Cool 5 minutes, unmold and cool fully. Glaze with confectioners' sugar, lemon juice and vanilla, set 30 minutes, and serve with the berry mix.",
"Faerie Fire|PAF": "Simmer sugar and water 5 minutes for syrup and cool. It keeps 2 weeks. In a punch bowl with large ice, mix white rum, dark rum, falernum, lemon juice, orange juice, pineapple juice, hibiscus tea, 3 ounces syrup and edible glitter. Rim glasses with pop rocks, add popping boba, pour the punch and garnish with rock candy.",
"Fey Fritters|HFFOTM": "Boil peas 2 minutes frozen or 3 to 4 fresh, chill in ice water and dry. Coarsely puree most, keeping ⅓ cup whole. Mix with eggs, milk, parsley, shallot, lemon zest, baking powder and seasoning, then fold in flour and feta. Fry 3-tablespoon rounds in oil on medium heat 2½ to 3 minutes, flip, and cook 1½ to 2 minutes. Keep warm at 250°F.",
"Feywild Eggs|HF": "Heat the oven to 400°F. Beat eggs with Parmesan, herbs, salt and pepper. Soften onion in a 10-inch oven-safe skillet about 3 minutes. Pour in the eggs and cook about 1 minute until the edges set. Top with diced cheese and bake about 14 minutes until puffed. Loosen, cool about 15 minutes and cut into wedges.",
"Feywine Punch|PAF": "Stir elderflower liqueur, grapefruit juice, lemon juice, honey and rose water in a pitcher until the honey dissolves. Add ice and the sparkling wine, stir gently and serve at once in rocks or stemless wine glasses.",
"Fig Cakes|HFFOTM": "Pulse almonds fine. Process figs with lemon zest, cinnamon, anise, salt and brandy for about 20 seconds, then pulse in the almonds. Roll six balls of scant ¼ cup each and flatten into ovals about 3 by 2 by ½ inch. Press the bottoms into sesame seeds. Rest sesame-side up for 1 hour before serving.",
"Fire-Spiced Abyssal Chicken Kebabs|HF": "Soak wooden skewers 20 minutes. Whisk molasses, lime juice and hot sauce. Coat chicken in chili powder, sugar, paprika, onion powder, salt and pepper. Heat a grill to medium-hot. Thread chicken, onion, bacon and oiled poblano on double skewers for eight kebabs. Grill about 15 minutes, turning every 3 minutes. Brush with the molasses mix and grill 1 minute per side. Rest 3 minutes and top with mint.",
}
